  "solution": {
    "text": "Following compounds are diamagnetic as in them metal ion has no unpaired electron.<br /><br />L: <math><mo>[</mo><mtext>Co</mtext><mfenced close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtext>N</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mtext>C</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>l</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br />M: <math><mtext>N</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>a</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mtext>Co</mtext><mfenced close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtext>Ox</mtext><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />O: <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mtext>Pt</mtext><mfenced close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtext>CN</mtext><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />P: <math><mo>[</mo><mtext>Zn</mtext><mfenced close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>(</mo><mtext>N</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br />In L, M, O inner d-electrons get paired while in P Zn has already <math><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup></math> configuration.<br /><br />In K and N there are 1 and 2 unpaired electrons respectively so they are paramagnetic.",
